## SOURCE
def first_value():String
  print("first-call\n")
  return "A"
end
def second_value(value:String):String
  print("second-call\n")
  return value
end
def main()
  let middle = "middle"
  print("<#{ first_value()}|#{middle}|#{second_value("B") }>\n")
end
## EXPECTED APPLICATION STDOUT
first-call
second-call
<A|middle|B>

## NOTE
Canonical EX-011 coverage for two effectful exact-String calls, leading-only and trailing-only ASCII SPACE padding, an identifier read between the calls, once-only source order, and existing String composition without conversion.
